 "note": "Quick, Draw! light bulb 6496968282996736. Stroke 3 is the glass: one round outline from the left neck up over the crown and down to the right neck. Stroke 4 is a single filament line inside the glass. Strokes 0, 1 and 2 are the three rings of the screw base, stacked under the glass. In the film the bulb itself does not move; the camera pulls back, so the bulb drifts left, gets smaller and settles lower on the table. The rig is rigid: the whole doodle is placed by two points, the top of the glass (crown) and the bottom of the screw base (base), so it changes size and place with the bulb and keeps its own proportions. No part turns.",
